# Adaptive & Responsive Design Upgrade

I have implemented a comprehensive update to ensure the GHG Reporting dashboard and calculation tools adapt perfectly to any screen size, from wide desktops to mobile phones.

## Key Improvements

### 1. Fluid Desktop Scaling
Resolved the issue where the dashboard appeared "larger than the browser" on smaller laptops.
- **Global Box-Sizing**: Applied `border-box` reset to ensure padding doesn't push elements beyond their intended width.
- **Auto-Fit Grids**: The dashboard grid now uses fluid `minmax` values, allowing it to scale naturally on 13" laptops and ultra-wide monitors.

### 2. Mobile Responsive Sidebar
Implemented a modern "Drawer" navigation for touch devices.
- **Hamburger Menu**: Added a sleek SVG toggle button to the top bar.
- **Drawer Animation**: The sidebar now slides in from the left with a smooth transition.

### 3. Integrated Facility Management
Moved the "Manage Facilities" settings directly into the [Custom Factors](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/custom-factors.html) page.
- **Consolidated View**: Users can now manage both custom measurement units and physical locations in one place.
- **Themed UI**: The facility forms and lists now use the same glassmorphism and dark theme as the rest of the dashboard.
- **Responsive Tables**: Facility lists adapt to mobile screen sizes with the same logic as custom factors.

### 4. Silent UI Experience
As per user preference, the application now provides a completely quiet user interface.
- **Alert Removal**: All `alert()` popups have been removed from the codebase.
- **Toast Silencing**: The global [toast.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/toast.js) system has been modified to log to the console instead of appearing on-screen.
- **Improved Focus**: Actions like saving, deleting, or importing now happen seamlessly without interrupting the user's flow with notifications.

### 5. Modernized Facility Selector
Enhanced the dashboard's navigation with a premium selection interface.
- **Icon Upgrade**: Replaced standard emojis with a custom Map-Pin SVG for a more professional look.
- **Premium Styling**: Added a glassmorphism container for the selector with smooth hover effects and a custom blue-hued dropdown arrow.
- **Consistent UI**: The new modernized selector is applied both to the main Dashboard and the Emissions Calculator filtering bar.

## Technical Details
- **CSS Breakpoints**: Tablet (`1024px`) and Mobile (`768px`).
- **Logic**: Centralized in [mobile-menu.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/mobile-menu.js) and [custom-factors.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/custom-factors.js).

## How to Test
1. **Desktop**: Navigate to "Custom Factors" to see the new "Manage Facilities" section below the factor form.
2. **Management**: Try creating or deleting a facility; it now updates instantly within the dashboard theme.
3. **Responsive**: Shrink the browser to verify the facility section stacks and scales correctly on mobile.
